    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7b9b5f13",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who are familiar with political humor, internet meme culture, and the use of animal-based ridicule to mock human institutions. The meme appeals to those who appreciate puns and absurd analogies, particularly those who find humor in the incongruity of equating a political body (Congress) with a group of baboons. The audience likely includes politically aware individuals who may be critical of or satirizing political institutions, as well as general internet users who enjoy edgy, sarcastic, or ironic content. The meme’s effectiveness relies on the audience’s understanding of the term 'congress' as both a political body and a collective noun for baboons, which is a niche but widely recognized internet joke. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of animal imagery with human governance, which resonates with audiences who are comfortable with degrading or mocking political discourse through animal metaphors.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e58cc306"
      },
